# Banana bread (the one that always works)

- 3 very ripe bananas, mashed
- 75 g melted butter
- 150 g sugar (less if the bananas are black)
- 1 egg, 1 tsp vanilla
- 1 tsp baking soda, pinch of salt
- 190 g flour
- optional: walnuts, chocolate chips

Mix wet, then dry, don't overmix. Loaf tin, 175 °C, 55–60 minutes, until a skewer comes out clean. Cool 10 minutes before turning out.

Froze well for two weeks in slices.
